# Kapur Lab — vsnp3 Step 2: per-group isolation (2026-07-19)
# Applies on top of v3.16-kapurlab-step2-read-length.patch. Idempotent via patch -N.
#
# One failing group no longer aborts the whole Step 2 run. group_on_defining_snps
# processes groups in two loops (FASTA/dataframe build, then RAxML tree/table via
# pool.map — which re-raises the first worker exception). Any error in one group
# (rare/degenerate lineage: empty df, bad alignment, RAxML/BioPython failure)
# would kill every other group's results. Now each group is wrapped: on failure
# it's flagged with a BUILD_ERROR marker and dropped from remove_list/working set,
# and the run continues so the groups that CAN finish — including the -a all_vcf
# set — still produce trees/tables. Also skips blank FASTA lines defensively.
